# GEM — Generative Ads Model / Generative Ads Recommendation Model

## Purpose

GEM (Generative Ads Model / Generative Ads Recommendation Model) is the platform's AI-powered advertising intelligence and optimization bounded context.

GEM is responsible for:

* Product advertising recommendations
* Product ad scoring
* Audience recommendations
* Creative generation
* Campaign recommendations
* Campaign optimization
* Budget recommendations
* Ad experimentation
* Performance analysis
* Advertising intelligence
* Conversion-oriented recommendations
* Automated advertising workflows
* Feedback and learning loops

GEM must integrate with the platform's existing Marketing, Catalog, Inventory, Order, Customer, Analytics, Promotion, Search, Notification, and Event/Queue infrastructure.

GEM must remain modular and provider-agnostic.

---

# 1. Architectural Position

GEM belongs primarily inside the Marketing bounded context but must have strict boundaries from other domains.

```text
Marketing
│
├── Campaigns
├── Promotions
├── Advertising
├── Social Media
├── Content
│
└── GEM
    ├── Product Intelligence
    ├── Audience Intelligence
    ├── Creative Intelligence
    ├── Campaign Intelligence
    ├── Budget Intelligence
    ├── Experimentation
    ├── Optimization
    ├── Recommendations
    ├── Automation
    └── Learning / Feedback
```

GEM is not the source of truth for:

* Products
* Prices
* Inventory
* Orders
* Payments
* Customers
* Financial accounting
* Promotions
* Tax
* Shipping

GEM consumes authoritative information from those bounded contexts.

---

# 2. Core Architectural Principle

GEM follows:

```text
Observe
  ↓
Analyze
  ↓
Recommend
  ↓
Validate
  ↓
Approve / Automate
  ↓
Execute
  ↓
Measure
  ↓
Learn
```

Never allow unrestricted AI-generated actions to directly mutate authoritative commerce data.

