# 61. Cursor AI Implementation Rules

When implementing GEM:

1. Inspect the existing repository before changing code.
2. Identify existing modules, domain boundaries, events, queues, repositories, authentication, RBAC, and admin UI patterns.
3. Reuse existing infrastructure.
4. Do not create duplicate Catalog, Inventory, Order, Customer, Analytics, or Finance models.
5. Do not bypass domain services.
6. Do not make Redis the source of truth.
7. Do not directly couple GEM to one AI provider.
8. Do not directly couple GEM to one advertising platform.
9. Use interfaces/ports for external providers.
10. Use Outbox + BullMQ for asynchronous workflows.
11. Make jobs idempotent.
12. Make external operations idempotent.
13. Add audit logging.
14. Add tenant/store/vendor authorization.
15. Add tests before declaring the feature complete.
16. Do not rewrite unrelated modules.
17. Preserve backward compatibility.
18. Follow existing project naming conventions.
19. Follow existing database migration conventions.
20. Follow existing API/error/validation conventions.

